"""
Fixed-pitch propeller driven by a piston engine, with the shaft speed as a
state.

# Why the shaft speed is a state

The obvious model, `T = eta*P/V`, is singular at zero airspeed and so cannot
be used for a take-off roll. Momentum theory fixes that but needs an implicit
solve for the induced velocity. Carrying the shaft speed instead keeps the
whole thing an ODE, gives a finite and correct static thrust, and comes with
throttle lag for free through the shaft inertia.

It also makes the engine-off case work without any special handling. With the
throttle closed the engine makes no torque, so the shaft is dragged round by
the airflow until the propeller's own torque vanishes, at `J = CP0/kP`. The
propeller then sits at a windmilling speed producing *negative* thrust --- the
drag of a windmilling propeller, which is exactly why a motor glider pilot
stops the engine before soaring.

Note there are then **two** engine-off equilibria: windmilling, and stopped at
`n = 0`, where both the torque and the thrust vanish. Which one a run finds
depends on the initial shaft speed. That is not an artefact --- a real stopped
propeller stays stopped until something spins it up --- but it does mean the
engine-off glide ratio depends on whether the propeller was left turning.

# Propeller model

Standard coefficients against advance ratio `J = V/(n*D)`, with `n` in
revolutions per second:

    T = CT * rho * n^2 * D^4          CT = CT0 - kT*J
    Q = CP * rho * n^2 * D^5 / (2*pi) CP = CP0 - kP*J

Both coefficients fall linearly with `J`, which is the usual behaviour of a
fixed-pitch propeller over its working range. Efficiency `eta = J*CT/CP` then
peaks near `J = 0.75`, as a wooden cruise propeller does.

# Engine model

A piston engine holds roughly constant torque over its range, so power rises
with speed. `torque_rise` gives the mild low-speed torque bulge real engines
show, and a smooth cut-off past `x_redline` stops the shaft running away --- at
full throttle and high airspeed the propeller unloads, and without the cut-off
there is nothing to limit the speed.

# Numerical conditioning

`n` appears in a denominator, so the advance ratio uses `sqrt(n^2 + n_eps^2)`.
That alone is not enough: a stopped propeller in fast forward flight drives `J`
to very large values and the linear coefficients with it, so `J` is saturated
smoothly with `tanh`. Both coefficients are then bounded for any combination of
airspeed and shaft speed, including reversed flow.
"""
component Propeller
  "Mount; thrust acts along the +x axis of this frame"
  frame_a = Frame3D() {^frame_a}
  "Density and wind"
  air = AirState() {^air}
  "Throttle, 0 is engine off and 1 is full power"
  throttle = RealInput() {^throttle}

  """
  Propeller rotation seen from behind looking forward. Sets which way the
  torque reaction rolls the airframe: a clockwise propeller rolls it left.
  """
  structural parameter clockwise::Boolean = true

  "Propeller diameter"
  parameter D::Length = 1.5
  "Rotating inertia of crankshaft and propeller together"
  parameter I_shaft::Inertia = 0.35
  "Rated shaft power"
  parameter P_rated::Real = 59700
  "Shaft speed at rated power, revolutions per second"
  parameter n_rated::Real = 45.0
  "Thrust coefficient at zero advance ratio"
  parameter CT0::Real = 0.135
  "Fall of the thrust coefficient with advance ratio"
  parameter kT::Real = 0.115
  "Power coefficient at zero advance ratio"
  parameter CP0::Real = 0.088
  "Fall of the power coefficient with advance ratio"
  parameter kP::Real = 0.048
  "Fractional torque bulge at low shaft speed"
  parameter torque_rise::Real = 0.15
  "Shaft speed at which engine torque is cut, as a multiple of rated"
  parameter x_redline::Real = 1.15
  "Sharpness of the redline cut"
  parameter M_redline::Real = 15.0
  """
  Advance ratio at which the coefficients saturate. Only there to bound the
  coefficients when a nearly stopped propeller meets fast forward flight; the
  `n_safe^2` factor already makes the *force* negligible there, so this can sit
  well clear of the working range. It must: windmilling settles at
  `J = CP0/kP`, about 1.8, and a tight saturation would distort the windmilling
  speed and hence the engine-off drag.
  """
  parameter J_max::Real = 6.0
  "Shaft speed regularisation, revolutions per second"
  parameter n_eps::Real = 0.5
  "Initial shaft speed"
  parameter n_start::Real = 0.0

  "Rated shaft torque"
  final parameter Q_rated::Dyad.Torque = P_rated / (2 * 3.141592653589793 * n_rated)

  "Shaft speed, revolutions per second"
  variable n::Real
  "Regularised shaft speed"
  variable n_safe::Real
  "Axial airspeed through the disc"
  variable V_ax::Velocity
  "Raw advance ratio"
  variable J_raw::Real
  "Saturated advance ratio used in the coefficients"
  variable J_adv::Real
  "Thrust coefficient"
  variable CT::Real
  "Power coefficient"
  variable CP::Real
  "Thrust, positive forward"
  variable T::Dyad.Force
  "Torque absorbed by the propeller"
  variable Q_prop::Dyad.Torque
  "Torque delivered by the engine"
  variable Q_eng::Dyad.Torque
  "Shaft power delivered"
  variable P_shaft::Real
  "Propulsive efficiency"
  variable eta::Real
  "Velocity of the mount relative to the air mass, world frame"
  variable v_rel_0::Velocity[3]
  "Velocity of the mount relative to the air mass, mount frame"
  variable v_rel_s::Velocity[3]
relations
  initial n = n_start

  v_rel_0 = der(frame_a.r_0) - [air.v_wind_x, air.v_wind_y, air.v_wind_z]
  v_rel_s = MultibodyComponents.resolve2(frame_a.R, v_rel_0)
  V_ax = v_rel_s[1]

  n_safe = sqrt(n^2 + n_eps^2)
  # Signed, smooth regularisation of V/(n*D): tends to the true advance ratio
  # for either sign of n and passes through zero rather than blowing up.
  J_raw = V_ax * n / ((n^2 + n_eps^2) * D)
  J_adv = J_max * tanh(J_raw / J_max)

  CT = CT0 - kT * J_adv
  CP = CP0 - kP * J_adv
  # `n*n_safe` is a smooth stand-in for `n*abs(n)`, so thrust and torque both
  # change sign with the direction of rotation and vanish at rest. Using
  # `n_safe^2` instead leaves the propeller torque positive even when the shaft
  # is turning backwards, and a stopped propeller with the throttle closed is
  # then driven to ever more negative speed without limit.
  T = CT * air.rho * n * n_safe * D^4
  Q_prop = CP * air.rho * n * n_safe * D^5 / (2 * 3.141592653589793)

  Q_eng = throttle * Q_rated * (1 + torque_rise * (1 - (n_safe / n_rated)^2)) *
          0.5 * (1 - tanh(M_redline * (n_safe / n_rated - x_redline)))
  P_shaft = Q_eng * 2 * 3.141592653589793 * n
  eta = J_adv * CT / max(CP, 1e-6)

  # Shaft dynamics. der(n) is in rev/s^2, hence the 2*pi.
  I_shaft * 2 * 3.141592653589793 * der(n) = Q_eng - Q_prop

  # Thrust along +x, and the torque reaction of driving the propeller. A
  # clockwise propeller takes torque +Q about +x, so the airframe feels -Q.
  frame_a.f = [-T, 0, 0]
  if clockwise
    frame_a.tau = [Q_prop, 0, 0]
  else
    frame_a.tau = [-Q_prop, 0, 0]
  end
metadata {
  "Dyad": {
    "icons": {"default": "dyad://Multtest/Propeller.svg"},
    "doc": {"behavior": false}
  },
  "_links": {
    "frame_a": {
      "Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": -50, "y1": 450, "x2": 50, "y2": 550}}}
    },
    "air": {
      "Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": 450, "y1": -50, "x2": 550, "y2": 50}}}
    },
    "throttle": {
      "Dyad": {"placement": {"icon": {"x1": 450, "y1": 950, "x2": 550, "y2": 1050}}}
    }
  }
}
end

"""
Propeller on a carrier driven at a constant airspeed, throttle wide open.

The shaft is released from rest and allowed to find its own equilibrium
against the propeller torque, which is the check that the engine and the
propeller are matched: the shaft should settle near its rated speed at cruise
and well below it when static.
"""
test component TestPropellerStatic
  world = MultibodyComponents.World(render = false) {^world}
  atm = Atmosphere(rho0 = 1.225) {^atm}
  mover = MultibodyComponents.PrescribedVelocity(r_start = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0], render = false) {^mover}
  prop = Propeller(D = 1.5, P_rated = 59700, n_rated = 45.0) {^prop}
  thr = BlockComponents.Sources.Constant(k = 1.0) {^thr}
  "Airspeed held through the run"
  parameter V_test::Velocity = 0.0
relations
  mover.v_x = V_test
  mover.v_y = 0
  mover.v_z = 0
  connect(atm.air, prop.air) {^id1}
  connect(thr.y, prop.throttle) {^id2}
  connect(mover.frame_b, prop.frame_a) {^id3}
metadata {
  "_links": {
    "world": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 40, "y1": 800, "x2": 140, "y2": 900}}}},
    "atm": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 540, "y1": 100, "x2": 640, "y2": 200}}}},
    "mover": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 240, "y1": 400, "x2": 340, "y2": 500}}}},
    "prop": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 560, "y1": 400, "x2": 660, "y2": 500}}}},
    "thr": {"Dyad": {"placement": {"diagram": {"x1": 540, "y1": 700, "x2": 640, "y2": 800}}}},
    "id1": {"Dyad": {"edges": [{"S": 1, "M": [], "E": 2}]}},
    "id2": {"Dyad": {"edges": [{"S": 1, "M": [], "E": 2}]}},
    "id3": {"Dyad": {"edges": [{"S": 1, "M": [], "E": 2}]}}
  }
}
end
